          "deepDive": "**〜すら** = *even ~*: it picks out an extreme (usually minimal) example to imply that everything else is true a fortiori: 昼休みすら取れない → *so of course I can't take a proper holiday*. It is a more written, slightly stronger version of **さえ**, and usually appears in **negative** contexts.\n\nParticles (＊ note): すら replaces が/を, but other particles stay in front of it: 夜が明けたこと**に**すら気づかない (気づく takes に), 家族**に**すら相談せず, 温泉**へ**すら (the やってみよう), 専門家**で**すら (で＋すら after a person as subject = *even an expert*; very common: 人ですら, 子どもですら). With embedded questions: 帰ったか**すら**, 再開されるかどうか**すら**.\n\nNuance in the やってみよう: the noun must be the *extreme* case. 南極へすら出かけかねない (Antarctica is the extreme destination for an 80-year-old; a hot spring is ordinary), 専門家ですら解けない (if even experts can't solve it, examinees surely can't), ジョギングすらしたことがない (jogging is the minimal case compared with 10 km), 上司どころか家族にすら (family are the people you'd least expect to be left out, so they are the extreme case after どころか).\n\nCompare:\n- **さえ** (N2): same meaning, more common; さえ also has the conditional use 〜さえ〜ば (*if only*), which すら lacks.\n- **も**: plain *also/even*, weakest.\n- **まで**: *even (to that extent)*, usually in affirmative, escalating sentences (子どもまで笑った).\n- **AはおろかBすら** (#24): すら frequently pairs with はおろか / どころか.\n- **Nだに〜ない** (#104, 微動だにしない): an even more literary *not even*, limited to fixed phrases.\n\nJLPT tip: 〜ですら (not 〜がすら) after a subject; すら is ✗ with ば-conditionals.",
